From: alvesmaicon <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sun4i-codec: speaker pin switch on the A23 card

sun8i_a23_codec_create_card() never sets card->controls, so there is no
way for userspace to mute the "Speaker" widget on its own. On a board
with no headphone jack detection, that means the speaker and headphones
always play together, with nothing to turn either one off.

The sun50i-h616 card in this same driver already solves this with
SOC_DAPM_PIN_SWITCH("Speaker"), which shows up in ALSA as a "Speaker
Switch" control. Wire the same thing up for the A23 card.

Not yet tested on real A23 hardware.

diff --git a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
index 93f511fb6..1c7d1b8f5 100644
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
@@ -1764,6 +1764,10 @@ static const struct snd_soc_dapm_route sun8i_codec_card_routes[] = {
 	{ "Right DAC", NULL, "Codec Playback" },
 };
 
+static const struct snd_kcontrol_new sun8i_a23_card_controls[] = {
+	SOC_DAPM_PIN_SWITCH("Speaker"),
+};
+
 static struct snd_soc_aux_dev aux_dev = {
 	.dlc = COMP_EMPTY(),
 };
@@ -1792,6 +1796,8 @@ static struct snd_soc_card *sun8i_a23_codec_create_card(struct device *dev)
 	card->dev		= dev;
 	card->owner		= THIS_MODULE;
 	card->name		= "A23 Audio Codec";
+	card->controls		= sun8i_a23_card_controls;
+	card->num_controls	= ARRAY_SIZE(sun8i_a23_card_controls);
 	card->dapm_widgets	= sun6i_codec_card_dapm_widgets;
 	card->num_dapm_widgets	= ARRAY_SIZE(sun6i_codec_card_dapm_widgets);
 	card->dapm_routes	= sun8i_codec_card_routes;
